  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the living conditions for displaced persons from Myanmar and host communities in Cox&apos;s Bazar district and Bhasan Char</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hosting nearly one million Rohingya people, Cox&apos;s Bazar in Bangladesh is one of the world&#x2019;s largest refugee settlements, comprised of thirty-three extremely congested camps. The need to support humanitarian operations has become more pertinent as the crisis protracts and the prospect of a safe, dignified and voluntary return to Myanmar remains unpredictable. This is reflected in the inter-agency Joint Response Plan for the Rohingya Humanitarian Crisis for 2024. In line with the Joint Response Plan and with support from the Government of Japan, IOM is implementing a 12-month programme to provide support to Rohingya refugees and host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar and Bhasan Char through site management and site development, shelter and non-food items, protection, water, sanitation and hygiene, disaster risk reduction, and social cohesion activities.</narrative>
  </description>
